# Model-driven UI

Dropdowns, create-nav labels, palette categories, and similar option lists are defined in `clay/model.json` and emitted by Clay into `client/src/generated/`.

## Do

- Add or change options in `clay/model.json` (`catalog.shell`, `catalog.connectorKinds`, Oscillator fields marked `modulatable`, and related catalog seeds)
- Run `clay generate` (or Clay MCP `clay_generate`) after model changes
- Import lists and helpers from `@/generated/catalog` (or other files under `client/src/generated/`)
- Render selects and nav by mapping those generated arrays

## Do not

- Hand-write option arrays (`{ key|id|value, label }` objects) in React or other client source outside `client/src/generated/`
- Import a hand-maintained `catalog.ts` mirror of the model
- Copy catalog values into local constants “just for the UI”

## Lint

`pnpm --dir client lint` runs `scripts/check-model-driven-ui.mjs`. Waive a rare case with:

`// earthbeat-ui: exception model-driven — <reason>`

